1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,900
Tesla's new car can fly.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:04,820
Yes.

3
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:06,900
Tesla's new car can fly.

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:09,090
And that's not even the genius part.

5
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:13,370
Tesla didn't just build a flying
car to sell you a flying car.

6
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:15,380
They built it to print money.

7
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:16,860
Let me show you how.

8
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:22,620
On Thursday, October 15th, at a SpaceX
facility in Texas, Tesla finally showed the

9
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:27,270
new Roadster, nearly nine years
after it was pitched in 2017.

10
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:30,910
They drove it up a ramp and launched
it over a row of other Tesla vehicles.

11
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,950
It spun in mid-air and
landed using thrusters.

12
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:39,700
Elon Musk said it can, quote, 'basically
fly like a rocket.' So how does it fly?

13
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:44,900
Tesla says it's cold-gas thrusters, the
same idea SpaceX uses on its rockets.

14
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:49,310
Compressed air from big carbon-fiber
tanks behind the seats shoots out of the

15
00:00:49,310 --> 00:00:50,160
nozzles.

16
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:51,600
There's a yoke wheel.

17
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:56,100
The Rocket is a one-seater, while the
Performance and Thrust are two-seaters.

18
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,830
And only the top trim gets
the full thruster setup.

19
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,970
The base Performance
version reportedly has none.

20
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,420
But how it flies is the easy question.

21
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,480
The better question is why build a
car that flies for a few seconds?

22
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,290
That answer is right
on Tesla's own website.

23
00:01:11,810 --> 00:01:15,450
The Performance model costs fifty
thousand dollars per reservation.

24
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:20,110
Five thousand up front, then a forty five
thousand dollar wire within ten days.

25
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,790
That's the road ready one.

26
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:26,250
The Thrust model costs two hundred and
fifty thousand dollars per reservation.

27
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:30,470
That's the limited one that
does 0-60 in 0.81 seconds.

28
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:31,670
And the Rocket?

29
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:33,000
Invite only.

30
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:35,480
You can't reserve it even
if you have the money.

31
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:36,990
Now here's the kicker.

32
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,790
Production doesn't start until 2028.

33
00:01:39,790 --> 00:01:43,340
So you pay TODAY, you MIGHT
get a car in TWO YEARS.

34
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,040
Now let's do the math.

35
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:47,830
Say two thousand people
reserve the Performance.

36
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:49,830
That's one hundred million dollars.

37
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:53,340
Say one thousand die-hard
fans reserve the Thrust.

38
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:55,180
That's two hundred and fifty million.

39
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:57,590
Three hundred and fifty million dollars.

40
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:01,810
If that were real, Tesla would be sitting
on that much of its customers' money,

41
00:02:01,810 --> 00:02:05,350
possibly interest free, for
a car that doesn't exist yet.

42
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:07,700
That's what I mean by printing money.

43
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:09,020
No bank loan.

44
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,040
No interest.

45
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,720
No giving up Tesla stock.

46
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:15,030
Just fans giving Tesla
a free loan for 2 years.

47
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:16,920
And they've done this before.

48
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:22,390
In 2017, Tesla took similar fifty and two
hundred fifty thousand dollar deposits for

49
00:02:22,390 --> 00:02:26,200
the Roadster promise, with
production due in 2020.

50
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:29,310
Nearly nine years later, some
people are still waiting.

51
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:32,350
Sam Altman reserved back in 2018.

52
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:36,410
He tried to cancel last year, had trouble
doing it, and it turned into an online

53
00:02:36,410 --> 00:02:37,650
feud with Musk.

54
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:40,530
Accountants call this
business strategy a float.

55
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:42,500
So why fly it this week?

56
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:45,040
Tesla's sales have been under pressure.

57
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:49,330
BYD has been outselling Tesla in Europe,
although its numbers include plug-in

58
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:50,220
hybrids.

59
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:54,820
And Tesla's third-quarter deliveries, about
four hundred eighty-six thousand, beat

60
00:02:54,820 --> 00:02:58,900
analyst expectations, but were still
down two percent from a year ago.

61
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:03,090
When your everyday cars aren't exciting
anyone, you build one that makes every news

62
00:03:03,090 --> 00:03:07,640
channel say 'Tesla is the future
again.' That's called a halo product.

63
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:09,040
Ferrari does it.

64
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:13,400
Almost nobody buys the flagship, but
it makes the normal cars feel special.

65
00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:15,840
Most people will never own the Rocket.

66
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:19,620
But now the car in your driveway feels
like it comes from the rocket company.

67
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:22,270
So, can Tesla's new car fly?

68
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,020
Technically, yes.

69
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:28,130
Real SpaceX thrusters, real
flight, and real results.

70
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:30,120
But the flight lasts seconds.

71
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:32,060
The deposits last years.

72
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:36,700
Tesla built a reason for you to hand
over fifty thousand dollars, years early.

73
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,330
That's Tesla's greatest marketing stunt.

74
00:03:39,550 --> 00:03:43,580
And if my math is even close, it just
printed them hundreds of millions of dollars

75
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:44,540
in one night.

76
00:03:45,110 --> 00:03:49,180
So, would you put fifty thousand dollars
down for a car you might have to wait years

77
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:49,810
for?

78
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,330
Tell me in the comments.
